   "body": "The lamp is named <em>amoris vile ministerium</em> — \"love’s cheap/base servant\". The object that should serve love has instead betrayed it; the contemptuous <em>vile</em> turns the helpful lamp into a treacherous menial.",
   "exam": "<strong>In an exam:</strong> \"Calling the lamp <em>amoris vile ministerium</em> is pointedly ironic: the humble servant of the lovers’ night has become the agent of their ruin, <em>vile</em> dripping with the narrator’s scorn.\"",
